meta {
  name: 04 - Submit Multiple Documents (Batch)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ocr/process
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  files: @file(../test_data_june/1000411295.jpg) @contentType(image/jpeg)
  files: @file(../test_data_june/1000411296.jpg) @contentType(image/jpeg)
  ~project_name: hr
  ~user_id: emp_1042
  ~document_type: AUTO
  ~async_mode: true
}

docs {
  Batch upload. The endpoint accepts a repeated `files` field (or a repeated
  `file` field - both are collected, and duplicates by filename are dropped).

  ## Response differs from the single-document form

  Async batch: success, total_documents, batch_requests, message - where
  batch_requests is an array of objects each holding filename, request_id and
  status. There is no top-level request_id; poll each entry separately with
  request 02.

  Sync batch: success, total_documents, and data as an array of full result
  objects.

  A client that assumes the single-document shape will break here, which is
  why this is a separate request rather than a note on 01.
}
